fwtest's USB host, two changes the unit asked for (HARDWARE-SPEC HW-176,
HW-177, HW-182). The first core's CON0 as read gives the lines' bits 16
and 17 (DM_SE, DP_SE) as a cable would: with no host they change from
read to read, in a fixed cycle that is never steadily 0; with the host
they read 0 until the device connects, then bit 17 set and bit 16 clear.
And the host checks FADDR two frames after the set-address request's
status stage, not at once, so a device that takes its address after the
status stage passes. The crate tests
`the_lines_wander_with_no_host_and_the_host_holds_them` and
`the_address_is_checked_after_the_status_stage` fail without it.
